			<div class="content" id="post-content-4182159">
									

<p>Kind of executed a bit weird, and I'm not really a big fan of how the joke was executed. I do see how the idea could be appealing with more work. Novote.</p>
<p>Also those email URLs really bug me, that's not how domains work. The TLD (top-level domain, like <tt>.com</tt> or <tt>.org</tt> or whatever) isn't going to be the department, either the Foundation has registered <tt>.scp</tt>, or they use the technically more correct but more boring <tt>.internal</tt> for private/internal networks. So your domains would be something like <tt>antimeme.foundation.scp</tt> and <tt>raisa.foundation.scp</tt> (or maybe their own domains, e.g. <tt>raisa.scp</tt>).</p>

